descriptionByLocale.en:
PUBLIC COMPETITION POLICY FOR ASSESSMENT (IDEALMENT BETWEEN 80%/32 HOURS AND 100%/40 HOURS) OF A INGEGNERE/A WITH SPECIALIZATION IN THE FURNITURE OF MOBILITY AND TRANSPORT

The MUNICIPIO DI LUGANO opens the public competition for the recruitment (ideally between 80%/32 hours per week and 100%/40 hours per week) of an engineer with specialization in the field of mobility and transport (described to procedures and planning studies - mobility and transport) at the planning, environment and energy division, mobility of the City of Lugano, under the conditions of the Organic Regulation of collaborators and collaborators. General requirements for ROCCL and in particular:

- unexceptionable conduct;

- Psychophysical fitness to function.

Special requirements

- diploma of engineer/academic degree or SUP or equivalent;

- specialization in the transport and mobility area, as an appropriate alternative and

proven practical professional experience in the field of mobility, traffic and/or transport;

- knowledge of planning procedures and publication of projects within the meaning of

Law on roads, instruments of higher order such as cantonal piano, Luganese agglomeration program, as well as the legal norms and bases on motorized individual mobility, public transport, slow mobility, postages, etc. or commitment to quickly acquire mastery;

- critical, organizational, planning, control, analysis and

propose and implement decisions;

- listening, interpersonal communication, mediation and negotiation and

availability to the user;

- precision, reliability, dispatch, compliance with terms and confidentiality in work;

- flexibility, autonomy, spirit of initiative and innovation, quality guidance,

practical sense and responsibility, ability to adapt and support high working rhythms;

- editorial, synthesis and relational capacity;

- attitude to both independent work and team;

- current use of major computer programs (Windows environment, MS package

Office, etc.);

- knowledge of traffic modelling applications (Visum, Vissim);

- availability of continuing training (updating and upgrading

professional); 2

- excellent knowledge of the Italian language (at mastery level/C1 or equivalent or

higher) and knowledge of German and/or French (at the level of autonomy/B1 or equivalent or higher);

- licence to conduct cat. B.

They constitute preferential title:

- recognition as a cantonal corporate mobility consultant;

- knowledge of GIS applications;

- membership of the Swiss Association of Engineers and Traffic Experts (SVI).

Planning, environment and energy, mobility Division Planning, environment and energy, mobility is responsible for the Regulatory Plan and more generally the issues with territorial impact, also dealing with mobility and transport policy, environmental and energy issues. The issues relating to the management of mobility and transport are declined in public transport, slow (cyclable and pedestrian) and individual motorized. The Mobility organizational unit optimizes, in collaboration with the cantonal authority and neighboring municipalities, the regional strategy of the Luganese Transport Plan (PTL) and the Bologna Road Plan (PVP), integrating the station management (posts) and proposing local measures. Mobility also assists the organizational unit Planning in the elaboration of the Urbanization Plans of the Regulatory Plans and participates in the publishing activities of procedures of the cantonal and local road projects, preparing the contents technically. Required from the profile of mobility applications for construction. On the basis of the work programmes, the needs of service and the priorities established by the managers, this professional figure processes and manages actions and projects in the field of urban planning, intercommunal or sectoral according to its objectives, both process and project, ensuring respect for costs, procedures, times and quality.

In particular:

